<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oregon Territory</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oregon Territory was an organised territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from 1848 to 1859, covering the present states of Oregon, Washington and Idaho and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a> and Wyoming. Created by Congress after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oregon-treaty">Oregon Treaty</a> and the Whitman massacre, it replaced the settlers' provisional government. Washington Territory was split off in 1853, and the western part became the state of Oregon in 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oregon-territory.jpg" alt="Oregon Territory" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uwe Dedering this file: Furfur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oregon_Territory_1848.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
